---
import { FOUNDER } from "../consts";
---

<section id="founder" class="px-6 py-20 lg:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div
      class="grid gap-12 rounded-3xl border border-pz-line bg-pz-paper px-6 py-12 sm:px-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-20 lg:px-16"
    >
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-pz-clay-strong"
        >
          Who built this
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-4 font-heading text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight md:text-4xl"
        >
          Built for one child first, by someone who does this for a living.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
          {FOUNDER.name} — {FOUNDER.role}, fifteen years building trading and
          wealth platforms at Deutsche Bank, Revolut and Capital.com, and a
          master's in computer and information systems security.
        </p>
        <a
          href={FOUNDER.site}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2"
          >batiaev.com</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
        <p>
          Parenza started as a private system for our own first child: routines
          logged every night, guidance checked against sources rather than
          forums, and a decision log recording what we chose and why. It ran for
          months before it was a product.
        </p>
        <p>
          Three habits from the day job ended up shaping it. Working with AI
          constantly, which is why Parenza plugs into the assistant you already
          use instead of demanding you move. Sitting through SOC 2, ISO 27001 and
          DORA audits in regulated businesses, which is why the{" "}
          <a
            href="/trust"
            class="text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2"
            >trust page</a
          >{" "}publishes control statuses instead of badges. And a professional
          reflex to validate a claim before acting on it — which is the whole
          reason specialists here cite what they're working from and say when a
          question needs a clinician.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/about" class="text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2"
            >Read the longer version →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-center text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">
      Employers are named as professional background only. Parenza is an
      independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by
      any of them.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
